hck: the `use_input_delim` flag requires the long name of `delim_is_literal`, not its clap id

clap 4 derive uses the field name as the argument id; `requires("delim-is-literal")` names the `--long`
spelling, which `cmd.id_exists` does not know. clap only checks `requires*` in `debug_asserts`, which
`cargo build --release` never compiles in; minicargo passes `--cfg debug_assertions` to every crate, so the
mrustc-built `hck` aborts in `Command::_build_self` before parsing any argument:
    Command hck: Argument or group 'delim-is-literal' specified in 'requires*' for 'use_input_delim' does not exist
Same text in every 0.11.x release (and already in 0.10.0).

--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@
     #[clap(
         short = 'I',
         long,
-        requires("delim-is-literal"),
+        requires("delim_is_literal"),
         conflicts_with("output-delimiter")
     )]
     use_input_delim: bool,
